  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be defined by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Then which of the following statements is(are) TRUE?</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jAiZj",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is decreasing in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tpgzQ",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is increasing in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sk2Vb",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is onto",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7jQF3",
      "text": "Range of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/0de6bb8c-70ea-48e9-a43f-3b29dca08fa0-image.png\" style=\"width: 140px; height: 58px;\" /></p><p>Hence, it is increasing in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>&#8746;</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Now as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>also,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/5db986cf-14a3-460c-b7d6-d0a97afbd93f-image.png\" style=\"width: 318px; height: 250px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, range is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>, and the function is into.</p>",
